Spectra — macOS app diagnostics and JVM-aware debugging.

Usage: spectra <subcommand> [flags] [args]

Global flags:
  --verbose, --debug   Log enhancement/collection failures to stderr (or set SPECTRA_DEBUG)
  --no-daemon         Do not use the daemon for alerts, whatswrong, load and idle

Subcommands:
  inspect    Inspect .app bundles (default; runs when no subcommand given) [macOS only]
  list       Inspect every .app under /Applications [macOS only]
  snapshot   Capture a structured snapshot of host + installed apps
  jvm        List or inspect running JVM processes
  db         Discover and inspect databases apps connect to (read-only; postgres, mysql, sqlite, mongodb, redis)
  toolchain  Show installed language runtimes and package managers
  network    Show current network state (routes, DNS, VPN, proxy, listening ports)
  power      Show current battery and thermal state
  thermal    Detect thermal throttling and CPU speed limits (exit 0 nominal, 3 warm, 4 throttled)
  impact     Compute the documented per-pid energy impact score from delta records
  devices    List Android devices/emulators (adb), booted iOS simulators, and emulator processes by worktree
  memory     Show memory pressure and swap (VM compressor on macOS; MemAvailable, PSI and zswap on Linux)
  storage    Show disk volumes and ~/Library footprint
  du         Show the largest directories and files under a path by allocated size
  fswatch    Watch a directory tree by polling and report which files and directories keep changing
  timemachine Show Time Machine status, destinations, and local snapshots [macOS only]
  services   Show launchd jobs and plist schedules [macOS only]
  startup    List what launches at login or boot; disable or enable user launch agents [macOS only]
  logs       Run bounded unified log queries [macOS only]
  updates    Show macOS install/update log entries [macOS only]
  system     Show system resource limits and saturation
  load       Admit, hold or back off a new job from load and memory, with per-worktree attribution
  uninstall  Plan (read-only) and apply a conservative app uninstall that moves only your own files to the Trash [macOS only]
  orphans    Find leftover processes (parent pid 1) whose working directory is under a worktree root
  process    List running processes sorted by memory (RSS)
  playbook   Show diagnostic playbooks and command plans
  diff       Diff two stored snapshots (alias for snapshot diff)
  rules      Evaluate recommendations rules against a snapshot
  issues     List, check, or update persisted issues from the recommendations engine
  baseline   Manage baseline snapshots (list, drop)
  fleet      Cross-host rollups: which hosts trip a rule, and version-drift matrices
  bisect     Find the snapshot where a rule started firing, and what changed alongside it
  reconcile  Print an advisory plan to make one host's toolchain match another's
  anomalies  Flag processes deviating from their rolling RSS baseline
  install-helper Install the privileged helper daemon (requires sudo)
  schedule   Schedule periodic snapshot capture via a launchd agent [macOS only]
  daemon     Manage the local per-user diagnostic daemon
  alerts     List, acknowledge, watch, and summarize daemon alerts
  sample     Collect a user-space CPU sample of a running process [macOS only]
  symbolicate Resolve raw stack addresses to symbol + file:line via atos [macOS only]
  spindump   Capture and summarize a per-thread stack report (heaviest stacks) [macOS only]
  vmmap      Summarize a process's memory composition by region (dirty/resident/swapped) [macOS only]
  vmregions  Composition by sharing/protection/backing, with RWX (W^X) flagging [macOS only]
  lsmp       Summarize a process's Mach port table (right counts, leak detection) [macOS only]
  whois      Attribute a busy XPC/Mach service to the client processes driving it [macOS only]
  owner      Who has this? Processes behind a port, an open file, a pid, or working under a directory (--under)
  idle       Find long-idle holders under a root: alive, near 0% CPU, no busy descendants (exit 3 when found)
  lineage    Show a process's ancestor chain and descendant subtree with RSS/CPU totals
  malloc-history Attribute allocations to call stacks (requires MallocStackLogging) [macOS only]
  flamegraph Render a native CPU flamegraph (SVG) from a process sample [macOS only]
  hang       Classify why a process's main thread is hung (lock/I-O/spin/idle) [macOS only]
  procdiag   Linux: diagnose a stuck or slow process from /proc (D-state, lock wait, fd leak, CPU spin, cgroup limits)
  pressure   Linux: show pressure-stall (PSI) and cgroup v2 memory/CPU/pids accounting
  timeline   Chronological incident timeline: process starts, unified-log errors, and installs
  spawns     Trace process starts and exits live to catch short-lived children (polling; misses processes shorter than --interval)
  memtrace   Sample a process's RSS over time (optionally its whole subtree) and say whether it is growing
  runtime    Identify a live PID's language runtime and the diagnostics available for it
  xattr-inspect Show quarantine, provenance, where-froms, and AppleDouble state of files
  core       Inspect crashed-process core files and suggest offline analyzers
  crash      Audit post-mortem readiness (can this machine produce a debuggable crash?)
  web        Diff an Electron app's app.asar payload between two versions
  whatswrong Ranked whole-system triage: why is this Mac slow right now?
  cache      Manage the local blob cache (stats, clear)
  version    Print Spectra version and exit
  capabilities Describe the machine-readable interfaces this build supports
  help       Show this help text

Flag-only invocations route to `inspect`:
  spectra /Applications/Slack.app
  spectra --all -v
  spectra list -v
  spectra --json /Applications/Cursor.app
